    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1989-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The intercepts are \\(\\frac{6}{a}\\) and \\(\\frac{6}{b}.\\) Therefore the triangle’s area is \\[ \\frac12\\cdot\\frac6a\\cdot\\frac6b=\\frac{18}{ab}=6, \\] which gives \\(ab=3.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is A.",
